    "attrs": {
      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span><span class=\"time\">20 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip warn\">Medium</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Greedy</span><span class=\"chip accent\">State-machine DP</span>\n    <a class=\"chip\" href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/best-time-to-buy-and-sell-stock-ii/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LC 122</a>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Best Time to Buy and Sell Stock II</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Unlimited trades, at most one share at a time. Any trade from day i to day j earns the sum of the daily changes between them, so the best plan simply collects every positive day-to-day change: <code>sum(max(0, p[d] - p[d-1]))</code>. O(n) time, O(1) space. The two-state DP (cash / hold) proves it and is the template for every other stock problem.</p>\n"
  },
